// Deal or Force - the de facto powers of 1 January 2024 (Scripts/Simulation/Factions.cs).
//
// Real organisations that held and governed ground of their own that morning without being
// recognised states. Each is cut out of the state it holds ground of: whole regions, and
// where a front ran through the middle of one, the provinces whose middle lies inside an
// area ring ([longitude, latitude] points). A province goes to the first faction that asks
// for it, so the narrow Turkish-held strips are written before the north-east that
// surrounds them.
//
//   relation     war / truce / peace with the parent on the first day
//   holds        the parent's ground it holds at war without owning it (occupied)
//   army_share   the share of the parent's formations that are really the faction's
//   patrons      the states that keep it going; the backers in a war are "sponsorships" below
//   parent_capital  where the parent government actually sat, when the war had moved it
//   parent_modifier a condition the war had put on the parent (common/modifiers), for as long
//                   as the faction's own "seasoned insurgency"
//   listed_by    the states that list it as a terrorist or sanctioned organisation: they never arm it
//   fighters     its own men under arms, stood up as formations of 15 000
//   claims_state it means to rule the whole country: with the government's capital and half
//                its ground in hand, the government falls and the faction becomes the state
//
// The lines are the lines of that morning, at the resolution of the province map: the
// Euphrates through Deir ez-Zor, the Sirte-Jufra line in Libya, the Hudaydah coast.
